<Project>

  <!-- Keeps packages.lock.json independent of the installed SDK patch (#137).

       The single-file analyzer (EnableSingleFileAnalyzer in gclo.Engine, gclo.ViewModels
       and gclo.Cli) makes the SDK add an implicit PackageReference to
       Microsoft.NET.ILLink.Tasks at the version of its own bundled runtime. global.json
       rolls forward to the newest 10.0 SDK (the KofTwentyTwo standard), so every SDK
       patch resolved a different version: a locked restore failed with NU1004, and an
       unlocked one rewrote three lock files.

       The implicit version comes from the SDK's KnownILLinkPack item; fixing it here
       pins the analyzer package like any other dependency. Keep it at the version
       bundled with the SDK named in global.json (the oldest SDK allowed to build this
       repository), never newer: analyzers built for an older compiler load in a newer
       SDK, not the reverse. After changing it, refresh the lock files (the restore
       command with force-evaluate, in CONTRIBUTING.md).

       This lives in Directory.Build.targets, not Directory.Build.props: the item is
       defined by the SDK's props, which are imported after Directory.Build.props. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <KnownILLinkPack Update="Microsoft.NET.ILLink.Tasks" ILLinkPackVersion="10.0.12" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
